  "contract": [
    "Only the acknowledged selected paginated 0.167 task can request turn or item pages.",
    "Page sizes are integers 1 through 100, descending only; turns request notLoaded items and item pages remain whole-thread reads.",
    "Opaque continuation cursors come only from that selected task and the same page family. Responses remain at most one MiB, 100 entries, and bounded retained cursor/turn inventories.",
    "Original account is checked before and after every page; malformed replies, workspace/account changes, cancellation and unknown operations refuse without delivery.",
    "Retained Windows channels use the same history validation and do not reinitialize or retire their native owner."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The demonstration uses the actual installed 0.167 CLI, production launch arguments, Python WebSocket handshake and relay with a synthetic provider; it is not live-account or actual IDE GUI acceptance.",
    "Native per-turn editing, anchor cursors, ascending requests and experimental methods remain refused. No prompt or provider tool effect is admitted by history support.",
    "Thirteen integration groups pass 136 tests with one existing skip. Final history and release-package groups pass 39 with zero skips after reviewing variable native page sizes. Counts overlap.",
    "The two earlier native missing-method refusals and original regression failure remain retained.",
    "Source changes are not yet installed. Complete Windows verification remains unsuccessful and separate."
  ]
